<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">.github/workflows/pr-test.yml</code>: <code class="notranslate">npx fred-ssr</code> → <code class="notranslate">npx --package=@mdn/fred fred-ssr</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">.github/workflows/pr-test.yml</code>: <code class="notranslate">npx rari …</code> → <code class="notranslate">npx @mdn/rari …</code></li>
</ul>
<h2 dir="auto">Motivation</h2>
<p dir="auto">Prevent dependency-confusion fallbacks in <code class="notranslate">npx fred-ssr</code> and <code class="notranslate">npx rari</code>.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Additional details</h2>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">npx &lt;bin&gt;</code> resolves to the local bin only when present; otherwise npm silently downloads and runs a registry package literally named <code class="notranslate">&lt;bin&gt;</code>. In CI, <code class="notranslate">npx</code> assumes <code class="notranslate">--yes</code>, so this happens with no prompt. <code class="notranslate">fred-ssr</code> is a bin of <code class="notranslate">@mdn/fred</code> and its bare name is unpublished (squattable); the unscoped <code class="notranslate">rari</code> name is owned by an unrelated third party, not MDN. Pinning <code class="notranslate">--package=@mdn/fred</code> / <code class="notranslate">@mdn/rari</code> guarantees the intended bins.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h2>
<p dir="auto">Part of <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4769189075" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1680" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/fred/issues/1680/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1680">mdn/fred#1680</a>.</p>]]></content>
